A||||6||Richard Parnell||Rear deck as wing||||1||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||11-06-2000||01:43 PM||||Seeing another post of a Fiero with the rear deck lid open reminded me of an idea I had some time ago.  I was thinking that you could use the rear deck lid as a wing and sort of air brake by having the deck powered by a hydraulic unit of some type.  What are others thoughts on this?  Would the deck going up (at a controlled rate activated by the speed of the car similar to some wings on VWs and Porsches) make the car totally unstable or would it work as I think it might?||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-06-2000||02:59 PM||||I would guess the turbulence of the air rushing through the open engine compartment would probably negate many of the benefits.<P>Anbd wind turbulence would probably destroy your decklid in short order.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||11-06-2000||03:10 PM||||An actuated wing would be kinda kool, but I don't think I would want the whole rear deck open and close.  Just my thoughts...<P>Hmmm..  are you planning on landing a Fiero on the deck of an aircraft carrier?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||11-06-2000||03:26 PM||||Some one was joking about making actuators to turn the spoiler vertical w/ and then put a mirror on the bottom of it. for use against tail-gaters. interesting idea, but I don't think it was ever comepleted.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||11-06-2000||06:05 PM||||Back in the 60s the Chevy Chaparral (sp?) had a variable incident wing that the driver controlled.  It was quite effective against the Ford GT40.||||reg||1
Z||000005||HAGS||11-06-2000||06:15 PM||||You drive a Fiero! come on, no one should be on your tail, you should be on theirs....Im considering making a "Slower Traffic Keep Right" sign to put on my car...maybe write it backwords so people can read it when im on their tail.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever2||11-06-2000||06:30 PM||||I would think the advantages would be offset by the extra weight of the hydraulic equipment.  Not to mention (well okay I will) the precious space it would use.<BR>||||reg||1
